  "result": "Perfect! Late fees are complete. All 278 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **lateFee(invoice, asOf)** function in src/reports.js that:\n   - Calculates late fee at 0.04% of the amount still due per day overdue\n   - Returns 0 if:\n     - Invoice has no due date\n     - Invoice is not overdue (asOf \u2264 dueDate)\n     - Due amount is 0 (fully paid invoice)\n   - Formula: `due * 0.0004 * daysOverdue`\n   - Uses `daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)` to calculate days overdue\n   - Uses `balanceDue(invoice)` to get the amount still owed\n   - Rounds result using `roundCents()` (banker's rounding)\n\n2. **12 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - No fee when not overdue (dueDate on/after asOf)\n   - No fee when asOf is before dueDate\n   - No fee for invoice without dueDate\n   - Fee calculations: 1 day (21\u00a2), 7 days (144\u00a2), 77 days (\u20ac15.84)\n   - Partial payments (fee on remaining balance only)\n   - Fully paid invoices (no fee)\n   - Small amounts (accurate rounding)\n   - Different payment terms (NET14, EOM)\n   - Invoices with line discounts\n   - Correct banker's rounding\n\nLate fees accumulate daily at a reasonable 0.04% rate (\u224814.6% annually), applied only to the outstanding balance.",
